{"kind":"request","text":"Claude: make the fold's per-receipt commitment capture cost independent of the log, so one cold fold of a deep workroom is much cheaper.\n\nhugh approved filing this on 2026-10-17, as step 2 of the design note for request c4c2be71 (notes/2026-10-16-signing-fold-once.md on request/signing-fold-once at ae22e0bc3).\n\nWhen the fold admits an effective merge receipt that carries merge_left_live or merge_changed_paths, it calls foldState.unsettledCommitmentEvents (internal/workroom/fold.go:686 and 2098@b81a80cf0). That call recomputes staleness for the whole graph and projects every commitment, to capture which commitments were still unsettled on the incoming frontier. The work grows with the log, and the fold repeats it for each receipt.\n\nMeasured on 2026-10-16, on a frozen artroom copy at depth 43,744 with 188 merge receipts: one fold costs 5.5 to 10 s, and 75 to 85 % of that is in this function. Every process that folds pays it: the resident's cold start, gs status, and each signing command, several times over.\n\nOutcome. A fold at artroom depth no longer spends most of its time recomputing the unsettled commitment set per receipt. The answer at each receipt and every projection stay exactly the same. No new persisted format, cache or trust is added.","body":{"conditions":"1. The report states one cold local fold's wall time and CPU on the frozen artroom copy at depth 43,744 before and after, with the share spent capturing unsettled commitments at receipts, from a profile. 2. The set each receipt captures equals the from-scratch unsettledCommitmentEvents answer: a test checks this at every receipt of a fixture that includes merges, retirements, supersessions and staleness changes, and goes red when the incremental answer is broken. 3. Projections are byte-identical to the current fold at the same frontier on the frozen artroom copy and on the gitseq log. 4. No persisted format, cache, profile advance or trust boundary changes; architecture.md is updated only if a stated fold contract changes. 5. go test ./... passes at the head.","target_head":"b81a80cf0274703bf839bb4ef711203a2f2fa11a","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}